{
  "title": "Question words, connectors and frequency words",
  "note": "Question words carry an accent: qué, quién, dónde, cuándo, cómo, cuánto, cuál, por qué. Without the accent, porque means because and cuando means when in a statement. Before es, use cuál for specific information (¿Cuál es tu nombre?) and qué for a definition (¿Qué es una tapa?). Frequency words like siempre and nunca usually go before the verb.",
  "src": {
    "t": "Spanish 1A: Beginning Spanish (LibreTexts)",
    "u": "https://human.libretexts.org/Courses/Chabot_College/Spanish_1A%3A_Beginning_Spanish_(2026)"
